---
const title = "Visibility Audits — measuring how AI answer engines represent B2B companies";
const description = "Holdout-controlled measurement of whether ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Perplexity name your company when buyers ask. Causal measurement, not activity tracking.";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://visibility-audits.com/" />
    <style>
      body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 36rem; margin: 4rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #1a1a1a; }
      h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; line-height: 1.3; font-weight: 600; }
      a { color: inherit; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>AI answer engines recommend vendors to your buyers. We measure whether you are one of them.</h1>
      <p>
        Most AI visibility tools report activity. We measure causation: a calibrated
        baseline, treatment with holdout prompts left untouched, then a retest — so a
        movement in citations can be attributed to the work rather than to the engine
        drifting on its own.
      </p>
      <p>
        Built for funded B2B companies with high-consideration purchases and a
        similarly-staged competitor.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:danny@visibility-audits.com">danny@visibility-audits.com</a>
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
